  <h3>Conclusion</h3><p>2024 became the “year of the pause” in India’s monetary policy history. The RBI’s cautious stance reflected the delicate trilemma of emerging markets — ensuring growth, anchoring inflation, and managing global volatility. For UPSC aspirants, it underlines the complexity of central banking in balancing competing objectives in a dynamic economy.</p>
